---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BRAND, sites, updated, longDate } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy | Tidy Magpie"
  description="What tidymagpie.com stores and what it does not: no accounts, no forms, no tracking and no cookies. Each Tidy Magpie site has its own privacy page."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <section class="page">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Short version: this site does not ask who you are, does not track you and stores nothing in your browser.
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>This site</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No accounts, logins or forms.</li>
        <li>No analytics or tracking scripts.</li>
        <li>No cookies, and nothing saved in your browser.</li>
        <li>The typeface is served from this site, not from an outside font service.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The other {BRAND} sites</h2>
      <p>
        Each site has its own privacy page, because each does slightly different things. Trackers and checklists save
        your progress in your browser's local storage and it is never sent to us. The aurora site can use a location
        if you choose to give it one, and its page explains exactly how.
      </p>
      <ul>
        {sites.map((s) => (
          <li><a href={`${s.url}privacy/`}>Privacy on {s.name}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        Pages are served by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes technical request data such as IP
        address and browser type in order to deliver pages and protect against abuse. See
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a> for how it handles that data.
      </p>

      <h2>If you email us</h2>
      <p>We receive your email address and whatever you write. It is used only to deal with your message.</p>

      <h2>If this changes</h2>
      <p>
        If what this site collects ever changes, this page will be updated first to say what is used, what it
        collects and how to opt out where that applies.
      </p>

      <p class="small muted">Last updated {longDate(updated)}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
